    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are looking for a high-ceiling performance today, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Jacob Wilson** (71.63), who project as our most potent assets. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against a pedestrian starter, carrying a +14% boost from his platoon advantage that cements his status as our primary engine. Meanwhile, **Jacob Wilson** faces an elite arm in Framber Valdez, but his profile is anchored by a significant park factor (+10%) and an assumed top-of-order role, keeping his daily efficiency well above the threshold. **Drake Baldwin** also warrants high-leverage consideration; his 70.05 score is bolstered by a strong xwOBA of 0.386 and a favorable matchup against Mikolas, positioning him as a high-efficiency leadoff option.\n\nOur toughest bench decision involved **Denzer Guzman**, who hovered at a 45.77 efficiency score\u2014surpassing our 40-point floor\u2014but ultimately missed the cut due to the \"Lineup Pending\" volatility and the strength of our starting outfield. **Miguel Vargas** was the most notable exclusion at 39.08, falling just short of the start requirement against Rasmussen. Risk management remains central to our strategy today, particularly concerning the left-handed trio of **Gunnar Henderson**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**; all three face a tough test against S\u00e1nchez and Mathews. While the wind-out conditions provide a slight +5% tailwind for **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**, their scores are throttled by the pitcher's skill level. Finally, we are keeping a close watch on **Heliot Ramos** and **Jacob Wilson**, as their assumed batting orders remain unofficial; any drop in lineup positioning would necessitate a re-evaluation of their production ceiling.",
